        "subject": "A bright steel pin tool joint coming down from under the dark gripper casting, with a saturated ember band across its middle. Its turned pin threads, with specular rings on each crest, seat into the counterbored mouth of a grey box held in a slip wedge at the rotary. Two bare slip handle rods angle up on either side.",
        "visual_consequence": "Threaded steel entering the box of a held joint, directly under a machine's casting with no hand in the frame. The band carries the motif from the cover, so the connection reads as made by the arm without the headline.",
        "weakness": "The band brightens steadily from its left edge to its right edge with no falloff at the silhouette. The slips are a plain grey trapezoid prism with two untextured rods and no visible cast at the rotary, and the joint steel has no wear.",
